--TEST--
A call to a loaded extension is type-checked against its manifest, so an argument of the wrong type does not compile — `rule:packaging/extension-calls-are-statically-typed`
--EXTENSION--
ledger
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `Shop\Ledger::echoInt` takes an `int`, and `echoList` takes an `array<int>`.
// Both calls below pass a string, so the program does not compile.
echo Shop\Ledger::echoInt("three"), "\n";
var $numbers = Shop\Ledger::echoList(["one", "two"]);
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `int`, found `string`
  --> case.nvs:4:27
%A
error[E0401]: expected `int`, found `string`
  --> case.nvs:5:39
%A
error[E0401]: expected `int`, found `string`
  --> case.nvs:5:46
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
